  "result": "`IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now clamps to a value inside the range. The full test suite passes: 1908 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Before, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`. It now gives `1`.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`: an open minimum (`-5` \u2192 `1`) and an open maximum (`50` \u2192 `9` with `max=10`).\n- **Changelog:** I didn't add an entry. `CHANGES.md` starts at the already-released 8.5.0 and has no unreleased section.",
